meta {
  name: Anyone: the hub, signing in, and what the access body publishes
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  What Regulation (EU) 2025/327 requires an access body to publish: the Art. 56
  information duty, the Art. 73 registers of permits and results, and the yearly
  activity report. Since #404 (ADR-044) every API route needs a session, so these
  are read signed in, with the collection's default session. Only requests 01 (is
  the hub up) and 06 (where to sign in) still go without one, because they are
  what makes signing in possible, and 07, the start page's TestFlight form,
  which visitors without an account send (ADR-048).
}
